From: Jacob Riff <jacob@riff.dk>
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] media: ipu-bridge: Add ST VD55G1 sensor for Lenovo X1 Carbon Gen 14

The IR camera on the Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 14 is an ST VD55G1
behind ACPI HID "TBE20A1" (sibling of the "TBE20A0" IMX471 RGB sensor
on the same machines). Single CSI-2 lane; 600 MHz link frequency
verified streaming on hardware (804x704 @ 30fps, Y10).

Identification: chip-id readback via the vd55g1 driver (model id
0x53354731), matching the sensor named in the tuning metadata of
Lenovo's Windows driver package for this ACPI ID.

Tested-on: Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 14 21V7CTO1WW, kernel 7.1.4
Signed-off-by: Jacob Riff <jacob@riff.dk>
---
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -100,6 +100,8 @@
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("SONY471A", 1, 200000000),
     /* Sony IMX471 (found on Lenovo X1 Carbon G14) */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("TBE20A0", 1, 200000000),
+	/* ST VD55G1 IR camera (Lenovo X1 Carbon G14) */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("TBE20A1", 1, 600000000),
 	/* Toshiba T4KA3 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("XMCC0003", 1, 321468000),
 };
